# Repomap — Cangjie enumeration on an ISOLATED .cj fixture
#
# Companion to cangjie_repomap.case. That case runs against the codrax
# repo itself (--repo .), where the only .cj files are the thirdparty
# tree-sitter corpus and the request keywords (extend / foreign func /
# public class) collide with codrax's own Go parser — so it exercises
# the source-discovery / RNE-C53 path. THIS case instead delivers the
# PR-0c fixture that case always referenced but never shipped
# (eval/fixtures/testdata/cangjie_minimal/), so the Cangjie parser is
# exercised on real .cj source files in a clean repo with no grep noise.
#
# Fixture layout (covers func / class / struct / extend / foreign):
#   main.cj          package demo.app    — public class App + main entry
#   cart/Cart.cj     package demo.cart   — public struct Item, public class
#                                          Cart, extend Cart { ... }
#   bridge/Bridge.cj package demo.bridge — foreign func native_add,
#                                          public class Bridge
#
# Ground truth pinned by the grader: the `extend` block, the foreign func
# `native_add`, and at least one of the demo.* package declarations must
# all surface — a vague "Cangjie supports OOP" answer fails.
ID="cangjie_repomap_fixture"
NAME="repomap Cangjie extend + foreign func + public class on isolated .cj fixture"
FIXTURE="eval/fixtures/testdata/cangjie_minimal"
QUESTION="仓库里有哪些 extend 块、哪些 foreign func 声明、哪些 public class？分别列出文件路径和符号名，并指出包路径（package 声明）。"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="extend native_add"
EXPECT_SECTIONS="package"
EXPECT_MATCHES_TEXT_REGEX='demo\.(app|cart|bridge)'
